      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-212061",
      ":question/problem": "Fill in the correct options below to solve the congruence $15x\u226111(mod59)$.Since $gcd(15, 59) =$\n{{field-1}},\nusing the extended Euclidean algorithm, we get\n\n\n$1 = 15 \\cdot ($\n{{field-2}}\n$) + 59 \\cdot ($\n{{field-3}}\n$)$.\n\n\nTherefore, expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $59$, the solution to the congruence is\n\n\n$x\u2261$\n{{field-4}}\n$(mod59)$."
